from pathlib import Path
import pandas as pd
p=Path(__file__).parent
s='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><title>August error diagnosis</title><style>body{font:15px/1.6 system-ui;max-width:1250px;margin:40px auto;padding:0 24px}table{border-collapse:collapse}td,th{padding:8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;text-align:left}</style><h1>August 2026 error diagnosis</h1><p><b>Conclusion:</b> Evidence points primarily to limited model responsiveness under more volatile daily load, rather than a demand merge or averaging error. This is a diagnosis of local archived inputs, not independent verification of all upstream observations.</p><h2>Data reconciliation</h2><p>All 2,976 July-August half-hours match the means of exactly six five-minute readings in the local AEMO PRICE_AND_DEMAND_202607_NSW1.csv and PRICE_AND_DEMAND_202608_NSW1.csv files. Maximum absolute difference is 0.000000334 MW (rounding). The source has unique timestamps. Interval endpoints are shifted back 30 minutes to match the model's interval-start convention. No demand gaps or duplicate model timestamps were found.</p><p>July temperature has 12 missing half-hours; August has 16 out of 1,488 (1.08%). There are zero and two inherited wind forward fills respectively. The largest error, August 9, has no missing temperature or filled wind. These checks do not show missing data as the main explanation. Available-reading daily summaries may still be imperfect.</p><h2>Monthly changes</h2>'''
s+=pd.read_csv(p/'monthly_diagnostics.csv').round(3).to_html(index=False,border=0)
s+='''<p>Mean absolute day-to-day changes in daily minimum increase from 366 to 820 MW; midday minimum changes increase from 548 to 1,032 MW. Midday PV changes increase from 345 to 899 MW. Greater variation makes yesterday-based and smoothed lag features less reliable. These are descriptive associations, not proof of weather causation.</p><h2>Controlled diagnostics</h2><p>Ridge alpha, preprocessing and targets are unchanged. No wind and No weather retrain on the same pre-April history. Refit through June extends training only through June 30. These diagnostic trials do not replace the selected model or earlier results.</p>'''
s+=pd.read_csv(p/'diagnostic_experiments.csv').round(3).to_html(index=False,border=0)
s+='''<p>Removing wind does not improve August. Removing all weather worsens it. Updating through June barely changes it. These results weaken wind-definition mismatch and stale training cutoff as the primary explanation, without proving the inputs error-free.</p><h2>Largest individual errors</h2>'''
a=pd.read_csv(p/'largest_errors.csv');s+=a[['Date','Target','Actual_MW','Prediction_MW','Error_MW','temp_missing','wind_filled','pv_mid_mean','pv_jump']].round(2).to_html(index=False,border=0)
s+='''<p>August 9: mean midday rooftop PV falls by 2,314 MW from the previous day, while actual midday minimum demand rises by 2,667 MW. The model predicts 5,211 MW against 8,281 MW observed. August 25 has a 3,026 MW PV decline and a 3,205 MW increase in midday minimum. The existing features include temperature, wind and lagged demand, but no same-day solar/cloud input. Within August, signed prediction errors correlate with mean midday PV at 0.84 (daily minimum) and 0.86 (midday minimum). These are post-hoc, 31-day correlations; they do not establish which weather event caused the changes.</p><h2>Important counter-evidence: adding PV alone is not a proven fix</h2><p>An explanatory trial adds observed mean midday PV to Ridge. To ensure fair comparison, both variants use exactly the same 813 pre-April days with complete PV (the 2024 gap is excluded). This is an oracle diagnostic, not operational forecasting: actual same-day PV is not known in advance.</p>'''
s+=pd.read_csv(p/'observed_pv_diagnostic_only.csv').round(3).to_html(index=False,border=0)
s+='''<p>August daily-minimum MAE improves modestly (608 to 561 MW), but midday error worsens (718 to 768 MW), and both July errors worsen. Therefore the evidence does not justify claiming that adding a simple PV column solves the problem. Interactions, changing solar capacity, regional representation and target nonlinearity remain hypotheses to test using training-period validation.</p><h2>Next experiment</h2><p>Retain August as an inspected diagnostic period. Investigate solar/cloud forecast inputs, season-specific behavior and nonlinear models using the original fixed validation dates. Judge improvements on independent future dates. Do not delete large-error days: source reconciliation gives no basis to classify these demand observations as corrupt.</p><h2>Reproduction</h2><p>diagnose_august.py reproduces the analysis from the desktop repository and desktop source data. source_reconciliation.csv contains the full local AEMO comparison. Existing notebooks, source data and test results were not edited. Source locations: Desktop/database/AEMO/2026-07/NSW1 and 2026-08/NSW1; Desktop/NSW1_Core_Study_Data_30min_20261014; repository data/provenance and data/combined.</p></html>'''
(p/'REPORT.html').write_text(s)
